  "implementation_choices": [
    "Windows are applied to the decision date p; a weekly decision needs a complete r5 (C[p+6] in the snapshot), so the last 4 sessions of the snapshot are not decision dates.",
    "Features are ranked within U3000 members per date (percentile rank - 0.5, average ties); log_mcap is ranked like the others (monotone in mcap > 0, else NaN).",
    "ind_code is used only for demeaning (labels, RFF columns, target weights), never as a model input.",
    "y21_rank = per-date percentile rank (0, 1] of the industry-demeaned hedged label; rows with missing forward prices have NaN label and are dropped from training.",
    "M3 RFF draw: omega ~ N(0, I_23) (2000 x 23), gamma_p uniform on {0.5..1.0} via default_rng(20261004) in the order omega, gamma; RFF columns are demeaned over all members of the date before dropping rows with a missing r5; N_t counts rows with finite r5; weeks with < 100 usable rows are skipped.",
    "z selection on the early weeks uses s_bar of that fit subset; the final refit uses s_bar of all training weeks; ties in validation Sharpe go to the smaller z.",
    "Permutation models: the GBDT permutation shuffles y21_rank among rows of each training date (rows with non-missing label); the M3 permutation shuffles r5 among all rows of each date, default_rng(1) in both cases; M3_perm runs the same z selection on its own factors.",
    "GBDT trio uses FamilyModel from run_t20260930_17_model_family_sweep unchanged (seeds, parameters, native NaN); m2 = mean of per-date average-rank percentiles of lgbm, xgb, cat.",
    "Rank IC against y21_rank uses Spearman on offset-0 dates that have a complete 21-session label; NW lag 4; autocorrelation is the median Spearman between consecutive offset-0 dates over common symbols; correlation with m0 uses offset-0 weekly simplified returns.",
    "Simplified returns use the unclipped beta-hedged r5 with beta from ctx.ewma.at(t) (NaN -> 1.0, clip [-1, 4]); NaN r5 -> 0; no short-eligibility, VIX or hedge-leg sizing.",
    "Signal-library standardized columns carry a constant for missing values (no NaN remains; e.g. 17% of bm, 98% of cmp_opp_buy_60d tie at one value), so after the per-date rank the ties get their average rank; no further imputation was done.",
    "Modal cost 0.6645 USD = smoke 0.0082 (first attempt, wrote to the wrong dir) + 0.0038 + train 0.6525 (actual_cost_usd_estimate from modal-ledger-actuals.jsonl, measured wall time)."
  ]
